 x6 up  in front of the office restaurant or  theater but the x6 is also impressive  off-road terrain that used to demand a  range rover is now open to this suv  coupe  the m-performance twin power turbo array  6-cylinder diesel engine in the bmw x6  m50d sets a new benchmark for combining  striking dynamics with astonishing  efficiency the advanced engine responds  extremely quickly  even at low rpms the engine has a lot of  torque and the revs range is especially  broad  typically for bmw the cockpit is  tailored to the driver clear arrangement  and top-notch craftsmanship are  convincing  the eight-speed steptronic sport  transmission adapts to the driver's  individual driving style ranging from  comfortable cruising to highly dynamic  sportiness all at the press of a button  with a steptronic transmission shifting  is extremely comfortable and as  efficient as possible  what we do is we have the associate who  takes his lift assist  and he comes to the rack and actually  has to pick up the ip  and the lift assist just helps him hold  the ip  and guide it to the car  they have to tighten their screws down  and then you have the associate in the  middle who finishes the process by you  know routing their electronic wires and  then they end up installing the radio  and the face plate on top of that  the standard bmw x6 chassis sets  standards bmw xdrive guarantees  outstanding traction on any surface and  any weather x-drive and the dynamic  stability control or dsc keep it driving  stably and on track  the intelligent all-wheel x drive  instantly distributes power to both  axles so the car touches the road  optimally thus the x drive combines the  advantages of all-wheel drive traction  stable handling and driving safety with  the agility typical of a bmw we are  loading the tires here we have the tires  come around just in time the tires will  come around the front tires first we'll  load it if it has a 2v8 option then  we'll load up a locking lug if not we'll  just put in five regular lugs and we  will go from there then the rear tire  come around we'll load it start those  and then torque them down with the  multi-spindle  in the bmw x6 m50d the engine the  chassis technology and the design work  seamlessly together with impressive  dynamics comfort and practicality  the new x6 is more angular than its  predecessor the chassis is a benchmark  the equipment blameless the x6 may look  more compact but it's still a powerful  4.9 meters long and weighs a good two  tons  the bmw x6 is built to move in germany  the price for this kind of mobility  begins at 66 150 euros if you like think  sporty the bmw x6 m50d is a good choice  that the volvo v60 plug-in hybrid has a  range of 50 kilometers so the driver  should recharge the battery at every  opportunity fortunately it has the  necessary cable in the trunk  he says this end plugs into the car  and the other goes into the outlet  sounds simple  but the cable is fitted with a special  plug  if it isn't compatible all the driver  can do is get out a cable reel and hope  for the best  but this particular volvo v60 plug-in  hybrid is already fully charged so the  test drive can begin when driving on its  diesel engine it puts out 208 kilowatts  with fuel consumption rated at 1.8  liters  running on electric power it can cover  50 kilometers free of emissions running  on both it can go 900 kilometers without  refueling it accelerates from zero to  100 kilometers per hour in 6.1 seconds  just sitting in it matas can hardly tell  any difference between the plug-in  hybrid and a standard v60 except that  the combination instrument cluster  includes a battery level indicator  alongside the fuel gauge and an  indicator for whether the car is running  on electricity or diesel  hybrid and power drive modes the power  mode as the name implies relies more on  the diesel engine giving the car more  power  with diesel farad  and if he needs to go easy on the  battery the safe button switches to the  diesel for long drives cross country or  on the highway and saves the battery  power for the stop and go driving  typical of the city  it's hard to tell any difference between  the plug-in hybrid and a standard v60  from the outside as well  the sporty look of the five-door station  wagon is brought out even more by the r  design dynamic attributes  chromed emblems identify the plug-in  hybrid as such  the trunk offers just 304 liters of  volume partly because of the space taken  by the recharging cable stowed under a  panel inside  the hybrid diesel's interior has been  kept in the traditional volvo style a  digital instrument cluster is standard  in the v60 d6awd  matas had to get used to the power  steering since the diesel engine doesn't  run continuously the steering isn't  hydraulic powered assisted as in the  standard v60 instead it's electric and  that has a different feel which takes a  few kilometers to adjust to  what's his overall impression after the  first few kilometers  mata says unfortunately the volvo v60  plug-in hybrid isn't as fuel-efficient  as the 1.8 liters per hundred kilometers  the car maker claims for it his average  of about 6.2 liters is far removed so  for a good 10 000 euros less he could  buy a standard v60 with the biggest  diesel engine in germany it consumes  about the same and has a bigger trunk  the second generation of the  mercedes-benz b-class will be hitting  showroom floors across europe in late  november over 380 000 units have been  sold worldwide since it was launched in  2011.  both interior and exterior have been  revamped a broad radiator shield and  daytime running lights integrated into  the headlights give the new b-class a  more dynamic look  electric drive and natural gas drive are  available  these days the automotive industry is  all about saving fuel and limiting  emissions porsche is no exception  putting out an se hybrid version of its  best-selling cayenne with consumption  rated at 3.4 liters per hundred  kilometers the plug-in can cover 36  kilometers at up to 125 kilometers per  hour on electric power alone the 82 000  euro list price in germany is almost two  thousand euros more than the cayenne s  this light green 224 kilowatt ford focus  rs belongs to dennis  he swears by it  when the ford focus came out in 2009 it  set new performance standards for front  wheel sports cars  especially in traction and handling it's  a compact class vehicle with a racing  car feel  our car tester dennis insect says this  car is awesome but now he's looking for  something more family friendly but he  doesn't want to compromise on sportiness  the sea at leon cooper 280 aspires to  the best of both worlds it's seatt's  speediest compact model  copious air intakes point to a powerful  engine under the hood  leon's trademark rear design as well as  the two tailpipes add to its dynamic  look  so dennis says it doesn't appear that  sporty at first glance  he likes the look of the headlights  and notes the wide tires  he notices the rear end is narrower  the exhaust and matching diffuser lended  a degree of sportiness dennis is excited  so  time to go for a spin  you can sense the cooper's sporting  lineage right away cooper stands for cup  racing a modified cooperative is among  the fastest front-wheel drives ever to  take the nurburgring's legendary  nordschleifer track  a limited slip differential improves  on-road performance the cooper offers a  range of driving modes  as far as dennis is concerned the modes  are only good to play around with  once you've chosen one you're likely to  stick with it the rest are mostly  designed for people who like to mess  around with buttons  our test car courtesy of dsg is equipped  with gear shift paddles  dennis says this car's shift pedals are  a bit small and you need rather long  fingers to keep your hands on the wheel  while changing gears he prefers shifting  manually which makes driving more fun  the two-round instruments and  three-spoke steering wheel with embossed  logo give the cooper's interior a sports  car feel as do the seats  dennis thinks the cockpit design is  visually appealing and uncluttered  despite being a little heavy on plastic  so how does driving the cupra compare to  the focus rs  dennis says the engine can't quite  compete but concedes that it falls only  marginally short on performance and  sportiness  a top speed of 250 kilometers an hour is  pretty standard for a car like the cupra  it moves from zero to 100 kilometers an  hour in 5.7 seconds its 206 kilowatts of  power is almost 20 less than dennis's  focus puts out  theoretically it should perform better  on the road  dennis says the cooper's traction is a  little worse when accelerating out of  curves than his ford has  he's got plenty of material to form an  impression of the leon time now for his  verdict  it's sporty he decides but it's not a  real alternative to the ford  a vinyl roof  abundant chrome trim  the finest leather and wood inlays it  must be a luxury car from the early  1970s  the jaguar xj coupet with its v12 engine  is quintessentially english blending  elegance and sportiness into one  at the 1973 london motor show the  british luxury brand rolled out a  four-seat coupe version of the xj it  launched five years before  the series familiar straight six engine  was standard with a v12 as a glorious  option  since it was made in very small  production runs the noble cat is rarely  seen on the open road these days or even  at vintage car meets  11 dealership appreciates the sleek  lines of the older car and the  12-cylinder engine's interaction with  the automatic transmission he says it's  nothing like the conventional power  trains of the time but he can hardly put  it in words  jaguar's 5.3 liter v12 was a legend  among car engines famous for its even  acceleration and silky smooth running  but among mechanics the car was more  infamous  he says the engine compartment looks  more like a snake pit he's got no  problem with the engine itself  it can run dependently for some 200 000  kilometers without an overhaul but he  doesn't like disassembling the entire  intake duct just to fix the air  conditioning maintenance is very time  consuming even if parts are relatively  easy to find but otherwise he says the  car is nothing to fear  jaguar unveiled the xj coupe in 1973  but it didn't appear in showrooms until  two years later it targeted the  individualists who could dispense with  four doors in favor of two but not with  the luxury of the jaguar sedan it was  based on  describes it as a car for the  connoisseur capable of high speeds  though without matching aerodynamic  design the grill is a bit small for his  taste but he likes the way this jag  glides along at 160 kilometers per hour  has no b-pillar so driving on country  highways with the windows down as  heavenly  the imitation leather vinyl roof is  typical of the 1970s  and having two fuel tank filler necks  near the rear windshield is typical of  jaguar  aside from the rear doors the coupe has  all the amenities of the sedan among  them a large trunk for that holiday on  the french riviera and space for four  people  the interior offers the obligatory  luxury ambience with fine wood paneling  around the dash and british connelly  leather on the doors and seats  in the mid 1970s an xj12 coupe cost the  equivalent of about 25 000 euros making  it jaguar's most expensive model  says it was a top car for a top price at  the time it cost about the same as a  small townhouse like plunking down 200  000 euros for a car today just as far  beyond the reach of ordinary mortals now  as it was then  we're not thinking not so much  parts are available for the xj but it  may take some intensive searching to  find a 12-cylinder coupe a in good  condition and it could easily cost the  same twenty five thousand euros it did  new  yen  explains that prices for the xj coupe  are climbing and they're much higher  than for 